Sort points by x ascending (ties by y descending) and for each point i scan points to its right maintaining the highest y seen so far that is <= points[i].y; count a point j when points[j].y is <= points[i].y but strictly greater than that running bound.

```typescript
function countEmptyPairs(points: number[][]): number {
  // copy and sort by x asc, tie y desc
  const pts = points.slice().sort((a, b) => (a[0] - b[0]) || (b[1] - a[1]));
  const n = pts.length;
  let ans = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    // we track the highest y-value seen so far that is <= pts[i][1]
    // initialize to -Infinity so the first qualifying point is counted
    let maxBelow = -Infinity;
    for (let j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
      const yi = pts[i][1];
      const yj = pts[j][1];
      // j is a valid B for A=pts[i] iff yj <= yi and there is no previously encountered
      // point with y in [yj, yi] (we ensure that by requiring yj > maxBelow)
      if (yj <= yi && yj > maxBelow) {
        ans++;
      }
      // any point with y <= yi becomes a potential blocker for later j's
      if (yj <= yi) maxBelow = Math.max(maxBelow, yj);
    }
  }

  return ans;
}

```

Store each vector as a list of (index, value) pairs for non-zero entries and use two pointers to compute the dot product in O(L1 + L2) time.

```typescript
class SparseVector {
  private vals: [number, number][]; // array of [index, value] for non-zero entries

  constructor(nums: number[]) {
    this.vals = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
      if (nums[i] !== 0) this.vals.push([i, nums[i]]);
    }
  }

  dotProduct(vec: SparseVector): number {
    let i = 0, j = 0;
    let result = 0;
    const a = this.vals;
    const b = vec.vals;

    while (i < a.length && j < b.length) {
      const idxA = a[i][0], valA = a[i][1];
      const idxB = b[j][0], valB = b[j][1];
      if (idxA === idxB) {
        result += valA * valB;
        i++; j++;
      } else if (idxA < idxB) {
        i++;
      } else {
        j++;
      }
    }

    return result;
  }
}

// Example usage:
// const v1 = new SparseVector([1,0,0,2,3]);
// const v2 = new SparseVector([0,3,0,4,0]);
// console.log(v1.dotProduct(v2)); // 8
